**8. Exception Handling in Tests** — `addNullSkuManualCatch()` (line 92)

```java
try {
    catalog.add(null, 1);
    fail("should have thrown");
} catch (Exception ex) {
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

Manual `try/catch/fail` is the pre-JUnit 5 pattern. It's fragile — catching `Exception` (too broad) can mask unexpected errors.

**Fix:** Use `assertThrows` (exactly like the clean test at line 117):
```java
@Test
void addThrowsOnNullSku() {
    IllegalArgumentException ex = assertThrows(
        IllegalArgumentException.class,
        () -> catalog.add(null, 1));
    assertTrue(ex.getMessage().contains("sku is required"));
}
```

